
------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Business Problem

Large enterprises face challenges in:

-   Regulatory compliance monitoring (SEC, FINRA, SOX, GDPR)
-   Internal policy adherence validation
-   Continuous control monitoring
-   Audit preparation and reporting
-   Cross-functional compliance coordination

Manual processes are: - Expensive - Error-prone - Slow - Not scalable

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 2. Proposed Solution

An AI-powered multi-agent compliance platform built using CrewAI that:

-   Ingests policies, regulatory documents, contracts, and internal
    artifacts with modern UI
-   Decomposes compliance requirements
-   Validates operational evidence
-   Flags risk gaps
-   Generates structured compliance reports
-   Provides executive-level dashboards

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 3. Architecture Overview

## 3.1 High-Level Components

-   CrewAI Orchestrator
-   Specialized Agents
-   Tooling Layer (RAG, APIs, DB connectors)
-   Memory Store (Vector DB)
-   Human Review Interface
-   Reporting Engine
-   Modern UI stack


## 3.2 Agents

### 1. Regulatory Analyst Agent

Extracts obligations from regulatory text.

### 2. Policy Mapping Agent

Maps internal policies to regulatory controls.

### 3. Evidence Validator Agent

Validates operational artifacts (logs, configs, reports).

### 4. Risk Scoring Agent

Scores compliance gaps using predefined risk models.

### 5. Executive Reporting Agent

Generates board-ready summaries.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 4. Technology Stack

-   Python 3.11+
-   CrewAI
-   LangChain (RAG layer)
-   OpenAI / Anthropic LLMs
-   FastAPI
-   PostgreSQL
-   Chroma / FAISS / Pinecone
-   Docker
-   AWS (ECS / EKS / Lambda)
-   Terraform

